# A vendor-context fixup applied on top of the upstream stable chain, when the
# reMarkable tree needs it. It is the smallest patch that makes a vendored variant
# of an upstream level apply -- the "patch of the patch" the build currently
# applies by hand for the eight port files, but expressed as one optional piece
# instead of as committed ports that bake a specific kernel version's rejects into
# the tree.
#
# When absent (the file is deleted or renamed), the derivation applies the chain
# to the tree as upstream wrote it, and the eight port patches plus the derived
# syscore revert are still the ones that make the tree compile. The fixup is for
# the case where a future chain level hits a vendor-context hunk that one of the
# eight does not cover, or where the eight stop being needed because the vendor
# tree catches up.
#
# BEFORE ADDING THIS FILE: do not author it by hand against the committed tree.
# Produce it from a real failed apply, as the smallest hunk set that changes the
# chain's rejects into an apply, and link the upstream level and the device that
# motivated it here.
#
# DO NOT keep this file in the tree unless it has a reason and a source. An empty
# placeholder that nothing references is exactly the kind of dead provenance the
# AGENTS.md provenance rule exists to avoid.

